## 6. Alerting Strategy

| Severity | Response Time | Example | Channel |
|----------|--------------|---------|---------|
| **P0 — Critical** | < 15 min | Site down, DB unreachable, auth broken | PagerDuty + SMS + Slack |
| **P1 — High** | < 1 hour | Error rate > 5%, p95 latency > 5s | Slack #alerts + Email |
| **P2 — Medium** | < 4 hours | Error rate > 1%, memory > 85% | Slack #monitoring |
| **P3 — Low** | Next business day | Slow queries, cache miss rate high | Slack #monitoring |

**Alerting Rules:**
- Alert on symptoms (user impact), not causes (CPU usage alone).
- Every alert must have a runbook or action — no "informational" alerts.
- Avoid alert fatigue: tune thresholds so < 5 alerts/day on average.
- Use Slack channels: `#alerts-critical` (P0-P1), `#monitoring` (P2-P3).

