## 8. Log Aggregation

```typescript
// ✅ Structured log format for aggregation (JSON lines)
// Every log line must include:
{
  "timestamp": "2024-11-15T10:30:00.000Z",
  "level": "info",
  "service": "my-app",
  "version": "1.2.3",
  "environment": "production",
  "requestId": "req_abc123",         // Correlation ID across services
  "userId": "user_xyz",             // When authenticated
  "message": "Order created",
  "metadata": {
    "orderId": "ord_123",
    "amount": 99.99,
    "items": 3
  },
  "duration": 145                    // Operation time in ms
}

// Send to: Datadog, CloudWatch, Elastic, Loki, or similar
```

**Log Aggregation Rules:**
- All logs must be structured JSON in production (no `console.log('something happened')`).
- Include `requestId` in every log for distributed tracing correlation.
- Retain logs: 30 days hot (searchable), 90 days warm, 1 year cold (compliance).
- Set up log-based alerts for: `level=error` spike, specific error codes, auth failures.

